package "main"

// Field access through an explicit deref — `(*p).x` where `p` is
// `*T` (a raw pointer to a struct) — currently returns a constant
// 0 instead of dispatching to the field load.  Discovered while
// auditing plan-pointers-to-iface-values.md Slice P.2.
//
// Root cause: `pkg/ir/gen_selector.bn` (`genSelector`) handles
// EXPR_SELECTOR with EXPR_IDENT / EXPR_SELECTOR / EXPR_CALL /
// EXPR_BUILTIN bases, but has no case for EXPR_UNARY (the
// `*p` deref form).  Falls through to the `return
// b.EmitConstInt(0, types.TypInt())` fallback.
//
// Workaround: write `p.x` instead.  Auto-deref handles raw and
// managed pointers transparently; only the explicit-`(*p).x`
// syntax misbehaves.
//
// Same bug shape afflicts every pointer kind, but `*T` is the
// simplest reproducer.  The iv-method-dispatch path
// (`(*p).Foo()` from Slice P.2) goes through a different IR-gen
// route (`isInterfaceMethodCall` -> `genInterfaceMethodCall`)
// that doesn't share this fallback.

type T struct {
	x int
}

func main() {
	var t T
	t.x = 42
	var p *T = &t
	println((*p).x)
}
